{"name":"Orange Grove","hex":"#fbaf8d","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Orange Grove","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A locality in the Gunnedah council area, central New South Wales, Australia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Orange_Grove"}],"entries":[{"title":"Orchard","blocks":[{"text":"An orchard is an intentional plantation of trees or shrubs that is maintained for food production. Orchards comprise fruit- or nut-producing trees that are generally grown for commercial production. Orchards are also sometimes a feature of large gardens, where they serve an aesthetic as well as a productive purpose. A fruit garden is generally synonymous with an orchard, although it is set on a smaller, non-commercial scale and may emphasize berry shrubs in preference to fruit trees. Most temperate-zone orchards are laid out in a regular grid, with a grazed or mown grass or bare soil base that makes maintenance and fruit gathering easy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Orchard_Lanes.jpg/330px-Orchard_Lanes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orchard"},{"title":"Orange Grove (1800 ship)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange Grove was probably of Danish origin. She first appeared in British records in 1800. She made one complete voyage as a slave ship in the triangular trade in enslaved people. The French captured her in 1804 during her second slave trading voyage after she had embarked slaves but before she could land them in the West Indies."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_Grove_(1800_ship)"},{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour of pigments, produced by mixing yellow and red. In the RGB colour model, it is a tertiary colour. It is named after the fruit of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delicatearch.png/330px-Delicatearch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_(colour)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Orchard_Lanes.jpg/500px-Orchard_Lanes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Orchard_Lanes.jpg/1280px-Orchard_Lanes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Orchard_Lanes.jpg/500px-Orchard_Lanes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Apple orchard lanes with apples fallen off the trees","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOrchard_Lanes.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Streuobstwiesen%2C_Blick_auf_Traufgang_und_Lochenh%C3%B6rnle.jpg/500px-Streuobstwiesen%2C_Blick_auf_Traufgang_und_Lochenh%C3%B6rnle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Streuobstwiesen%2C_Blick_auf_Traufgang_und_Lochenh%C3%B6rnle.jpg/1280px-Streuobstwiesen%2C_Blick_auf_Traufgang_und_Lochenh%C3%B6rnle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Streuobstwiesen%2C_Blick_auf_Traufgang_und_Lochenh%C3%B6rnle.jpg/500px-Streuobstwiesen%2C_Blick_auf_Traufgang_und_Lochenh%C3%B6rnle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Meadow orchard (Streuobstwiese) with view to the Lochenhörnle [de]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStreuobstwiesen%2C_Blick_auf_Trauf